ures","content":"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"},"298":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-33","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#default","content":"Start with a labeled group of related values. Add selection or removal when\nthe group needs interactive behavior."},"299":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-34","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#toggle-chips","content":"Use Toggle Chips for multiple peer filters. Selected items show a check while\nunselected items remain available in the same group."},"300":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-35","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#removable-chips","content":"Use Removable Chips for user-added filters and tokens. Removing a Chip calls\nthe group callback so the owning collection can update its items."},"301":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-36","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#controlled-selection","content":"Use `selectedKeys` and `onSelectionChange` when another part of the page\nneeds to own the selected filter state."},"302":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-37","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#sizes","content":"Compare the supported `sm`, `md`, and `lg` sizes. Keep one size per group."},"303":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-38","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#disabled","content":"Disable individual options with `disabledKeys` when some values are unavailable."},"304":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#truncation","content":"By default, long labels truncate visually when space is constrained, while\nthe complete accessible value remains available."},"305":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#empty-state","content":"Give an empty collection useful guidance, then let the user add the first\nvalue. Removable items continue to be owned by the collection."},"306":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#menu-filter-trigger","content":"Use `ChipButton` for a menu trigger that shares the Chip family's compact\nsizing and presentation."},"307":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"Use a plain string for a simple Chip label. When content is composed, use\n`Text` for the visible label and `textValue` for the complete accessible value."},"308":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"Set the size on `ChipGroup` to share it with every Chip. `ChipList` wraps items\nhorizontally by default, and its layout props can be customized when needed."},"309":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"For removable Chips, provide `onRemove` on the group and add a self-closing\n`Button` with `slot=\"remove\"`. The callback receives a `Set` of removed keys;\nupdate the collection owned by your application."},"310":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#customization","content":"For Toggle Chips, use the Chip render prop to show a selected accessory."},"311":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#menu-filter-button","content":"When you need a menu with a Chip-like appearance, use `ChipButton` inside\n`MenuTrigger`. The menu trigger owns open state, focus, keyboard interaction,\nand `aria-expanded`; the consumer owns any configured-filter state."},"312":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Use `Label` or `aria-label` to name the `ChipGroup`; this names the collection,\nnot its individual Chips."},"313":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Give each Chip a visible label, `textValue`, or `aria-label`. Use `textValue`\nwhen a Chip contains icons, composed content, or a render prop."},"314":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Use a descriptive group label so removal actions can be announced clearly."},"315":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"Keep the visible label and the accessible value synchronized."},"316":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#accessibility","content":"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."},"317":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Keep labels concise and let them truncate only when the available width requires it."},"318":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Prefer groups of three or more related values."},"319":{"id":"/docs/components/chip-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chip#best-practices","content":"Keep one size per gr