gs":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#menugroup","content":"MenuGroup"},"737":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-19","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#menuitem","content":"MenuItem"},"738":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-20","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/menu#submenutrigger","content":"SubmenuTrigger"},"739":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-21","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu","content":"An accessible dropdown menu built on React Aria. It supports grouping with optional\ntitles, multi-select checkbox items, leading icons, submenus, and two sizes. It\nreuses Antares' `Popover` for the overlay and `Checkbox` indicator for selection."},"740":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-22","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Grouping with an optional title via `MenuGroup`, plus `MenuSeparator` dividers"},"741":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-23","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Multi-select groups: set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` on a `MenuGroup` to render\nits items as checkboxes, while other groups stay plain action items"},"742":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-24","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Optional leading `icon` per item; links (`href`) and disabled items"},"743":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-25","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Submenus via `SubmenuTrigger`"},"744":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-26","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Two sizes (`sm`, `md`); set `size` explicitly on each submenu `Menu`"},"745":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-27","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#features","content":"Usable anchored to a trigger or standalone (e.g. inside a bottom-sheet `Drawer`)"},"746":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-28","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#default","content":"A trigger with plain action items."},"747":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-29","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#controlled","content":"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."},"748":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-30","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#bottom-sheet","content":"On small screens a menu often reads better as a bottom sheet than an anchored\npopover. Since `Menu` works standalone, drop it into a bottom `Drawer`."},"749":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-31","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#groups","content":"Labeled groups separated by dividers, a multi-select checkbox group mixed with\nplain action groups, leading icons, a disabled item, and a link."},"750":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-32","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#multiple-selection","content":"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` renders its items as checkboxes.\nDrive the checked items with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or\nseed them uncontrolled with `defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each\n`MenuItem`'s `id`."},"751":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-33","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#rich-content-from-an-item","content":"A `Menu` is a collection, so it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger` children. Rich content inside a `Menu`\nor submenu is not supported. To show a `Calendar`, let the item close the\nmenu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored to the trigger\nwith `triggerRef`."},"752":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-34","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#single-selection","content":"A `MenuGroup` with `selectionMode=\"single\"` lets one item be selected at a time.\nDrive it with `selectedKeys` + `onSelectionChange` or seed it uncontrolled with\n`defaultSelectedKeys`. Keys correspond to each `MenuItem`'s `id`."},"753":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-35","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#sizes","content":"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."},"754":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-36","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#submenu","content":"Nested menus via `SubmenuTrigger`."},"755":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-37","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Space/Enter**: activate an item; **Escape**: close"},"756":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-38","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Arrow Up/Down**: move between items; **Home/End**: first/last"},"757":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-39","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Arrow Right/Left**: open/close a submenu"},"758":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-40","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"**Type to select**: jump to a matching item (string labels are used as `textValue`)"},"759":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-41","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#accessibility","content":"Multi-select items use RAC's `menuitemcheckbox` role; the checkbox indicator is\ndecorative (`aria-hidden`) and the item owns interaction"},"760":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-42","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Give each selectable `MenuItem` a stable `id`, and provide the `Menu` an\n`aria-label` when there is no visible label."},"761":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-43","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Use a leading `icon` for recognition, not as the only label - keep a text label."},"762":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-44","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"Reserve checkbox groups for multi-select; use plain groups for one-shot actions."},"763":{"id":"/docs/components/menu-45","page_id":"/docs/components/menu","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/menu#best-practices","content":"A `Menu` is a collection: it only renders `MenuItem`, `MenuGroup`,\n`MenuSeparator`, and `SubmenuTrigger`. For rich content (a `Calendar`, a form),\nclose the menu from `onAction` and open a separate `Popover` anchored with\n`triggerRef` instead of putting it in a submenu."},"764":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"page","content":"MetricsLockup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup"},"765":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-0","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","content":"The MetricsLockup component displays a single metric with an optional title, info tooltip, trend indicator, and description."},"766":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-1","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#installation","content":"Installation"},"767":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-2","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#examples","content":"Examples"},"768":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-3","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#default","content":"Default"},"769":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-4","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#with-trend","content":"With Trend"},"770":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-5","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#compact","content":"Compact"},"771":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-6","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"772":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-7","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"773":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-8","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"ARIA"},"774":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-9","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"775":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-10","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#props","content":"Props"},"776":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-11","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","content":"MetricsLockup displays a metric value prominently, with an optional title and tooltip for context, an optional trend icon to show direction of change, and a description label below the value."},"777":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-12","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#default","content":"A metric with a title, info tooltip, value, and description."},"778":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-13","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#with-trend","content":"Use the `trend` prop to show a directional icon next to the description. Accepts `'positive'`, `'negative'`, or `'neutral'`."},"779":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-14","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#compact","content":"Use the `compact` prop to render the metric value and description inline rather than stacked."},"780":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-15","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Key"},"781":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-16","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Description"},"782":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-17","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Tab"},"783":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-18","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the info trigger button and shows the tooltip"},"784":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-19","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Escape"},"785":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-20","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#keyboard","content":"Closes the tooltip"},"786":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-21","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The info trigger button uses `aria-label=\"More information\"` to describe its purpose."},"787":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-22","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The tooltip uses `role=\"tooltip\"` and is associated with the info trigger via `aria-describedby`."},"788":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-23","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#aria","content":"The info trigger has a minimum touch target of 44×44px, achieved via a CSS pseudo-element, to meet WCAG 2.5.5."},"789":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-24","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"Keep tooltip content concise and informative."},"790":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-25","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"The `data` prop accepts strings or numbers — format currency and percentages before passing them in."},"791":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-26","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."},"792":{"id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup-27","page_id":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metrics-lockup#best-practices","content":"`trend` is intended to accompany `description` to provide temporal context (e.g. \"↑ +3% vs. last month\"). A trend icon alone, with no description, leaves the direction unanchored (\"up since *when*?\"). If `description` is not provided, `trend` has no effect."},"793":{"id":"/docs/components/modal","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"page","content":"Modal","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal"},"794":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-0","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"The Modal component presents a dialog window over the page that focuses the user's attention on a single task or piece of information."},"795":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-1","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#installation","content":"Installation"},"796":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-2","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#examples","content":"Examples"},"797":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-3","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#default","content":"Default"},"798":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-4","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"799":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-5","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#scrollable","content":"Scrollable"},"800":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-6","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#triggerless","content":"Triggerless"},"801":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-7","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"802":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-8","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#keyboard-interaction","content":"Keyboard interaction"},"803":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-9","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#aria","content":"ARIA"},"804":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-10","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"805":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-11","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#props","content":"Props"},"806":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-12","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."},"807":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-13","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#default","content":"Compose a Modal from a `Heading slot=\"title\"`, a `CloseButton`, `Content`, and a\n`ButtonGroup`. `ModalTrigger` opens the Modal and manages its open/close state."},"808":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-14","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#controlled","content":"Pass `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` to `ModalTrigger` to control the open state externally."},"809":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-15","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#scrollable","content":"When the content is taller than the viewport, the `Content` region scrolls while the title\nrow and the `ButtonGroup` stay pinned."},"810":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-16","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#triggerless","content":"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."},"811":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-17",